# Phase 2 CLI acceptance — operator reference-corpus path (QV-015, ADR-0114)

`QAI_DATA_DIR` points the real `qai` binary at a fresh temp database (set by the
harness); each `console` block runs in order against that one database.

A reference-less import records the QV-015 skip (`reference_comparison:
skipped`). Supplying `--reference` makes the family evaluable: the operator
sees `reference_comparison: pass`, and a mismatch fails closed with a non-zero
exit and no edition staged.

```console
$ qai db migrate
migrations applied; schema version 21

```

```console
$ qai quran import ../../fixtures/quran/test-edition-min/manifest.json
imported test-edition-min@0.1.0 to Staged
note: synthetic test data — non-canonical (ADR-0101 fallback)

```

```console
$ qai quran activate test-edition-min@0.1.0 --yes
activated test-edition-min@0.1.0 (generation 1)

```

```console
$ qai quran verify
QURAN VERIFY
counts: pass — 2 checks pass
addressing: pass — 4 checks pass
unicode: pass — 1 checks pass
checksums: pass — 3 checks pass
roundtrip: pass — 1 checks pass
reference_comparison: skipped — reference comparison skipped: no reference corpus configured (ADR-0114; OD-03 owner gate)
exit: 0

```

The companion synthetic reference is byte-identical to the rich fixture and its
declared pins match, so the comparison is evaluated and passes.

```console
$ qai quran import ../../fixtures/quran/test-edition-rich/manifest.json --reference ../../fixtures/quran/test-edition-rich/reference.json
imported test-edition-rich@0.1.0 to Staged
note: synthetic test data — non-canonical (ADR-0101 fallback)

```

```console
$ qai quran activate test-edition-rich@0.1.0 --yes
activated test-edition-rich@0.1.0 (generation 2)

```

```console
$ qai quran verify
QURAN VERIFY
counts: pass — 2 checks pass
addressing: pass — 4 checks pass
unicode: pass — 1 checks pass
checksums: pass — 3 checks pass
roundtrip: pass — 1 checks pass
reference_comparison: pass — 1 checks pass
exit: 0

```

```console
$ qai quran verify --json
{
  "addressing": {
    "checks": [
      "quran.edition_active",
      "quran.ayah_identifiers",
      "quran.division_coverage",
      "quran.basmala_policy"
    ],
    "gate": "exit::OK",
    "status": "pass",
    "summary": "4 checks pass"
  },
  "checksums": {
    "checks": [
      "quran.edition_checksum",
      "quran.structure_hash",
      "quran.token_order_hash"
    ],
    "gate": "exit::OK",
    "status": "pass",
    "summary": "3 checks pass"
  },
  "counts": {
    "checks": [
      "quran.surah_count",
      "quran.ayah_count"
    ],
    "gate": "exit::OK",
    "status": "pass",
    "summary": "2 checks pass"
  },
  "reference_comparison": {
    "checks": [
      "quran.reference_corpus"
    ],
    "gate": "exit::OK",
    "status": "pass",
    "summary": "1 checks pass"
  },
  "roundtrip": {
    "checks": [
      "quran.token_roundtrip"
    ],
    "gate": "exit::OK",
    "status": "pass",
    "summary": "1 checks pass"
  },
  "unicode": {
    "checks": [
      "quran.unicode_form"
    ],
    "gate": "exit::OK",
    "status": "pass",
    "summary": "1 checks pass"
  }
}

```

An incompatible reference fails the run closed with exit 3 and leaves no
edition staged (the identity fixture is never imported elsewhere, so the
operator sees only the reference-comparison failure).

```console
$ qai quran import ../../fixtures/quran/test-edition-identity/manifest.json --reference ../../fixtures/quran/test-edition-rich/reference.json
? 3
error: QV-015 reference comparison failed for [..]; see the validation report

```
